# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# A static export has no server, so next.config.ts's redirects() is never
# called. This file is the only place redirects are defined. Cloudflare reads
# it from the root of the published directory.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. The first matching line wins, so the specific
# rules come before the wildcards. Cloudflare allows 2,100 rules, of which 100
# may contain a splat or a placeholder.

# --- Canonical host ---------------------------------------------------------
# www is a second address for the same site; fold it into the bare domain.
# Requires www.unitflip.org to be added as a custom domain on the Pages project,
# otherwise nothing resolves there for this rule to catch.
https://www.unitflip.org/* https://unitflip.org/:splat 301!
http://www.unitflip.org/* https://unitflip.org/:splat 301!

# --- Old URLs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The privacy page moved to /privacy-policy when the legal pages were added.
/privacy /privacy-policy 301

# --- Trailing slashes -------------------------------------------------------
# The build emits /length, not /length/. Strip the slash so a linked or typed
# trailing-slash URL resolves to the canonical one rather than 404ing.
/*/ /:splat 301
